Z||000018||frontal lobe||11-07-2001||10:23 PM||||I'm just speculating here, and TRYING to give people the benefit of the doubt.<P>Perhaps the thought is like when a loved one dies, you don't want to see tons of pictures of them everywhere to remind you all the time for a while, until there is some time to heal the pain. <P>Perhaps they just want it to be a WHILE of not having the WTC in people's faces while the pain is so fresh in people's minds.<P>But I don't think the intent is anything like wanting to forget it happened.<P>Just speculation and something to consider.  I don't necessarily say I agree with it either, just that if that is the motive then I can understand it at least.||||reg||1
