Z||000021||Ken Wittlief||11-08-2001||10:39 AM||||its not sticking our heads in the sand.<P> we bury our dead for more than one reason.<P> and we bury them in a cemetary, not in our front lawns.<P> what happend was a shock to all of us.<P> but we cant live a normal life in a constant state of shock.<P> so, just like when a loved one dies, there is a funeral, there is a time of greiving, there is a day of putting their things away in the attic, and then we move on.<P> from time to time we remember our fallen loved ones - but not every day, and not all day long. That would be cruel.||||reg||10
