Z||000023||Mach10||11-08-2001||06:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>its not sticking our heads in the sand.<P> we bury our dead for more than one reason.<P> and we bury them in a cemetary, not in our front lawns.<P> what happend was a shock to all of us.<P> but we cant live a normal life in a constant state of shock.<P> so, just like when a loved one dies, there is a funeral, there is a time of greiving, there is a day of putting their things away in the attic, and then we move on.<P> from time to time we remember our fallen loved ones - but not every day, and not all day long. That would be cruel.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, but you don't pull the photos off the wall, and you don't change the subject when someone mentions his/her name. Don't dwell on it, but you NEVER try to ignore it... See what I'm saying?<BR>||||reg||7
